{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":78828472,"ns":0,"title":"Approximately continuous function","extract":"In mathematics, particularly in mathematical analysis and measure theory, an approximately continuous function is a concept that generalizes the notion of continuous functions by replacing the ordinary limit with an approximate limit. This generalization provides insights into measurable functions with applications in real analysis and geometric measure theory.","description":"Mathematical concept in measure theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}